# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#  Agent Loop — configuration
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
#  Copy this file to  ~/.agent-loop.env  and edit it.  (Point AGENT_LOOP_ENV at
#  a different path if you want it somewhere else.)
#
#      Windows   copy agent-loop.env.example %USERPROFILE%\.agent-loop.env
#      macOS/Linux   cp agent-loop.env.example ~/.agent-loop.env
#
#  KEEP IT OUTSIDE ANY GIT REPOSITORY. The dispatcher checks out task branches
#  and resets the working tree, so a token file living inside a repo can be
#  swept into a commit. The default location is your home directory for exactly
#  this reason.
#
#  Format: KEY=value, one per line. No `export`, no shell expansion, no
#  multi-line values. Quotes around a value are stripped. Lines that are not
#  KEY=value (comments, blanks) are ignored. A value already present in the
#  real process environment WINS over this file.
#
#  Every setting below has a working default except the two marked REQUIRED.
#  Delete the lines you do not need — an absent key is the default.
#
#  The "Agent Loop: Set up / reconfigure ClickUp" command writes the first few
#  of these for you and leaves everything else you have typed here untouched.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────


# ═══ 1. REQUIRED ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

# Your ClickUp personal API token.  ClickUp → Settings → Apps → API Token.
# This is a secret. The file is written with 0600 permissions by the wizard.
CLICKUP_TOKEN=pk_your_token_here

# The ClickUp List that acts as the board and the state machine.
# There is deliberately NO default: a checkout that forgets this must fail
# loudly rather than start driving somebody else's board.
# Find it in the list URL: https://app.clickup.com/<team>/v/li/<THIS NUMBER>
AGENT_LOOP_LIST_ID=


# ═══ 2. YOUR REPOSITORY ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════

# Repository the loop works on. The VS Code button pins this to the folder you
# have open, so you normally leave it unset. Set it only to run the dispatcher
# by hand from somewhere else.
#AGENT_LOOP_REPO=

# Branch that task branches fork from, and that reviewers diff against. The loop
# never merges INTO it: a landed task is pushed to its own branch and integration
# is human-gated. So a finished task's code is on its branch, not here — which is
# why the Blocked By edge below decides whether a successor can see it.
#AGENT_LOOP_BASE=main

# Optional per-project prompt addendum: a short, imperative list of standing
# rules appended verbatim to every implement and review prompt. This is how a
# project injects its own conventions without any project text living in the
# extension. See examples/agent-loop.contract.example.md.
# Default: <repo>/tools/agent-loop.contract.md, silently skipped if absent.
#AGENT_LOOP_CONTRACT_FILE=


# ═══ 3. VERIFICATION GATE ════════════════════════════════════════════════════

# Test command run against the reviewed commit before it is allowed to land.
# Empty (the default) skips verification entirely — reviews still happen, but
# nothing independently proves the suite is green.
# It runs in a sandbox checkout with credentials stripped, NOT in your tree.
#AGENT_LOOP_VERIFY=npm test

# Where that sandbox lives. It is a persistent checkout reused by every verify
# (not a fresh clone), so installed dependencies survive between runs.
#AGENT_LOOP_VERIFY_SANDBOX=~/.agent-loop-verify-sandbox

# Comma-separated, repo-relative paths copied from your real repo into the
# sandbox ONCE, when it is first created. Use this for gitignored dependency
# directories — a git checkout never materializes them, so without this a
# verify fails every run on a missing-dependency error unrelated to the diff.
#AGENT_LOOP_VERIFY_SEED_DIRS=node_modules,vendor,.env.testing

# Environment file the verify run loads before executing your suite — use the
# SAME one CI uses. Read by examples/agent-loop-verify.example.mjs; if your
# AGENT_LOOP_VERIFY is a plain command instead, load the file yourself.
#
# Why this exists: whatever the verify process exports WINS over the non-forced
# env declarations in your test config (phpunit <env> defaults to force="false",
# pytest-env and dotenv behave the same). Pin a database variable anywhere in
# that chain and the suite quietly runs on a different engine than CI and
# production, so a green verify proves nothing about production. Nothing here
# hardcodes an engine — name your own file and the values come from it.
#AGENT_LOOP_VERIFY_ENV_FILE=/absolute/path/to/.env.testing


# ═══ 4. BOARD VOCABULARY ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#
# The dispatcher never hardcodes your workflow. These are the status and custom
# field NAMES it expects on the list; override any that your board spells
# differently. Run "Agent Loop: Check the ClickUp board" to validate them.

#AGENT_LOOP_STATUS_READY=ready
#AGENT_LOOP_STATUS_CODING=coding
#AGENT_LOOP_STATUS_REVIEW=in review
#AGENT_LOOP_STATUS_CHANGES=changes requested
#AGENT_LOOP_STATUS_BLOCKED=blocked
#AGENT_LOOP_STATUS_STALLED=stalled
#AGENT_LOOP_STATUS_APPROVED=approved
#AGENT_LOOP_STATUS_COMMITTED=committed

# Statuses the loop must NEVER pull work from, on any path — your planning
# column, where a human parks work that is not yet fully specified.
# Comma-separated. Both spellings ship by default on purpose: a status name is
# something a human can retype, and a guard that fails open on a typo is worse
# than no guard.
#AGENT_LOOP_STATUS_NEVER_PICKUP=planed,planned

# Custom fields on the list. Both are plain text fields.
#   Acceptance Criteria — what the task must satisfy; drives the review verdict.
#   Blocked By          — task ids this one waits on (native ClickUp
#                         dependencies work too, and are preferred for subtasks).
#                         This edge also picks the fork base: a successor forks
#                         from its predecessor's branch, which is the only place
#                         the predecessor's code exists until a human integrates.
#                         Omit the edge and the successor forks from the base
#                         branch without its prerequisite; leave two finished
#                         predecessors on separate branches and no single base
#                         holds both, so the task parks on `blocked` naming them.
#AGENT_LOOP_AC_FIELD=Acceptance Criteria
#AGENT_LOOP_BLOCKED_BY_FIELD=Blocked By

# Written by the setup wizard. Not read by the dispatcher — it only builds the
# "Open list in ClickUp" deep link.
#AGENT_LOOP_TEAM_ID=


# ═══ 5. AGENT COMMANDS ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#
# How each CLI is invoked. Override when a vendor changes flags, when you want a
# different model, or when the binary is not on PATH under its plain name.
# An agent whose command fails is treated as "down" and the loop routes around it.

#AGENT_LOOP_CLAUDE_IMPLEMENT=claude -p --model sonnet --permission-mode bypassPermissions --max-turns 40
#AGENT_LOOP_CLAUDE_CMD=claude -p --model sonnet
# Used only for the re-scope diagnosis of a task that has churned without
# converging — the one genuinely hard judgment call in the pipeline.
#AGENT_LOOP_CLAUDE_RESCOPE_CMD=claude -p --model opus
#AGENT_LOOP_CODEX_CMD=codex exec --sandbox workspace-write -c model_reasoning_effort="high"
#AGENT_LOOP_CODEX_PROBE_CMD=codex exec --sandbox read-only --skip-git-repo-check
# {pf} is replaced with the prompt-file path.
#AGENT_LOOP_GROK_CMD=grok --prompt-file "{pf}" --always-approve --no-plan --max-turns 40 --output-format plain


# ═══ 6. TIMING AND LIMITS ════════════════════════════════════════════════════

# Seconds between passes in --watch mode.
#AGENT_LOOP_POLL=60

# How many failed review rounds a task may churn before it is escalated —
# one Claude re-scope diagnosis, then either back to ready or parked as stalled.
#AGENT_LOOP_MAX_ROUNDS=5

# Terminal progress tick during long agent stages, in seconds. 0 disables it.
#AGENT_LOOP_HEARTBEAT_S=30

# Per-stage caps, in seconds. Defaults are measured from real runs, but the
# right value depends on your suite. Raise the verify cap for a slow full-suite
# gate; a lane killed at the buzzer looks identical to a lane that is stuck.
#AGENT_LOOP_IMPLEMENT_TIMEOUT_S=1200
#AGENT_LOOP_REVIEW_TIMEOUT_S=600
#AGENT_LOOP_VERIFY_TIMEOUT_S=1500

# Plumbing timeouts and retry policy.
#AGENT_LOOP_GIT_TIMEOUT_S=120
#AGENT_LOOP_CLICKUP_TIMEOUT_S=30
#AGENT_LOOP_CLICKUP_TRIES=3
#AGENT_LOOP_CLICKUP_BACKOFF_MS=2000

# Upper bound, in hours, on how long a rate-limited agent is considered down
# before it is probed again.
#AGENT_LOOP_QUOTA_BLACKOUT_CAP_H=6


# ═══ 7. STATE FILE LOCATIONS ═════════════════════════════════════════════════
#
# All default to your home directory. Change them only if you want state
# somewhere else — for example to run two loops against two different boards.
# The VS Code button reads these three so its status matches the dispatcher.

#AGENT_LOOP_LOCK=~/.agent-loop.lock
#AGENT_LOOP_STOP=~/.agent-loop.stop
#AGENT_LOOP_STOP_REPORT=~/.agent-loop-stop-report.md
#AGENT_LOOP_LOG=~/.agent-loop.log
#AGENT_LOOP_ROUNDS=~/.agent-loop-rounds.json
#AGENT_LOOP_APPROVED_SHA=~/.agent-loop-approved-sha.json

# Path to THIS file. Only useful in the real environment (setting it inside the
# file it names has no effect). Use it to keep more than one configuration.
#AGENT_LOOP_ENV=~/.agent-loop.env


# ═══ 8. ESCAPE HATCH ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

# The dispatcher fences itself and refuses to start when a previous run ended
# with an agent having touched the primary repository — a state that needs a
# human to look at the tree. Set this to 1 for ONE run to clear that fence,
# after you have inspected it. Do not leave it set.
#AGENT_LOOP_UNSAFE=
